cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sector Connectivity and the Quantitative Modulus of Asymptotic Graviton Tomography"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Libo
date-released: 2026-09-14
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  An exact graph-theoretic classification of informational completeness for asymptotic
  observable algebras at future null infinity, together with a sharp quantitative modulus.
  The completeness modulus is identified with the algebraic connectivity of a
  coherence-transfer Laplacian; for the spin-4 Stokes connector this Laplacian is half an
  su(2) adjoint Casimir, giving spectrum lambda^2 k(k+1) and a spectral gap of exactly
  2 lambda^2 independent of graviton number. The same gap reduces the contested question of
  infrared memory superselection to an order-of-limits distinction. All results concern free
  asymptotic radiative data; the black-hole information paradox is not solved.
keywords:
  - asymptotic symmetries
  - null infinity
  - operator algebras
  - graviton tomography
  - BMS
  - infrared structure
